=09=09Stroke =20
=09=09
=09=09A stroke occurs when a part of your brain loses blood flow. This can =
occur=20
from a blockage of a blood vessel or a bleeding vessel in the brain. Sympto=
ms=20
are varied and usually start abruptly. They can include, but are not limite=
d=20
to, sudden numbness or weakness, difficulty speaking, a decrease or loss in=
=20
vision, headache, difficulty walking, or dizziness. Often the symptoms affe=
ct=20
only one side of the body. Prompt treatment may be able to prevent permanen=
t=20
damage. It is therefore extremely important to call 911 immediately, even i=
f=20
the symptoms have resolved.
=09=09
=09=09- Marc Ellman
