d=20
Web experience -- all text, for instance, or special low-graphics Web pages=
.=20
It's expensive, too. Most wireless Internet devices are Net-capaable cell=
=20
phones and PDAs, though more and more laptops and palmtops are offering=20
wireless modems. Wireless is still for road warriors and others who need it=
=20
at this point, but not for long. Telephone carriers, cell companies, and IS=
Ps=20
are teaming up to make wireless Internet service cheaper and more common.=
=20
Some even foresee an entirely wireless future. You'll be able to surf the N=
et=20
wherever you are, and make phone calls, too. As bandwidth grows, you'll eve=
n=20
get television and other multimedia entertainment over wireless devices.=20
Displays will get larger and brighter, batteries more efficient, and wirele=
ss=20
pipes fatter (can you still call it a "pipe" when it comes through the air?=
).=20
It's all going to happen, and sooner than you think.
