Hi Cooper,
I forgot to tell you, I did some FTR analysis back at the beginning of the year which was really interesting.  I also did some hydro flows analysis to forecast when the runoff would start picking up.  I did this by looking at previous years unregulated flows and average temperatures for Spokane and Kalispell and discovered that the flows increase dramatically approximately two months after the average temps reach above freezing on a continuous daily basis.  In addition to the Cal ISO OASIS conversion, I'm currently working on a webpage that will allow individuals to sign up for various e-mail alerts/notifications.  I'm also studying the load/resource balance and tweaking it to make it faster (i.e. through indexes, rewriting SQL code to promote optimization, etc.), more robust, and fully automated (through Perl and S-Plus).  
