>
>ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Involved in trading of energy, specifically power.
>Identify and evaluate current power market needs, supply
>availability, and new market opportunities. Ability to perform shift-work
>(5:30am-5:30pm or 5:30pm-5:30am). Excellent phone skills. Strong
>desire to learn trading.
>
>ESSENTIAL REQUIREMENTS: Advanced Excel spreadsheet skills. Bachelor's
>degree, preferably in a financial or economic discipline.
>Trading experience is a plus. Knowledge of Risk Management tools. Knowledge
>of trading products, regional forward price curves, risk
>management, pricing strategies, power supply, and transmission/physical
>assets to execute/facilitate transactions. Knowledge of regions in
>which power is traded (SERC, ECAR, PJM, MAIN, NY Power Pool).
