2. INVESTMENT IDEAS
A tale of two values
This pair of wireless infrastructure stocks offers long-
term growth--don't let the prices fool you

By Ben Mattlin, equity research columnist

Over the past two years, as the market's become more
challenging, investors are learning to be more selective than they
used to be. Rather than seizing momentum and growth, which
worked well in the '90s, successful investors are adopting a value
orientation.

But which discounted stocks represent true value and which are
inexpensive simply because the company they symbolize is no
good? In telecom, where most stocks have gotten hammered, it
can be especially difficult to distinguish between duds bargains.
