2. INVESTMENT IDEAS
Biotech rules
Biotechnology stocks point investors to a holy grail

By Michael Hickins, managing editor

On one level, it makes perfect sense for investors and analysts to favor
biotechnology stocks as much as they do: everyone wants to live forever,
and in relative physical comfort. Biotechnology offers the promise of a
rational (as opposed to mythical) Fountain of Youth, a picture of Dorian
Gray that never ages.

Moreover, biotechnology offers the potential to generate immortal
returns. Indeed, historical returns for the sector have been very
encouraging. According to analysts at U.S. Warburg, the industry has
been able to grow its collective top line by 18 percent since 1996. And
during the past 20-plus years, also according to the firm, the industry has
produced more than 100 drugs (using a wide definition of "biotech
drug"), "that currently generate annual revenues of roughly $12.5
billion."
