1. INVESTMENT IDEAS
Lost illusions
Wall Street's coming-of-age of investment theory

The real world doesn't always behave as expected. Law school graduates
are familiar with the expression which says, "'A' students become judges.
'B' Students become lawyers. 'C' students become rich."

The same could be said of the investment field.

Indeed, people in every walk of life have their own stories about how the
real-world methods of functioning often fail to follow theoretical ideas
about the way things ought to be done.
