2. INVESTMENT IDEAS
Top picks for 2002
Winning stocks will be switch-hitters and versatile utility players

By Robert Maltbie, Jr., CFA

Flexibility and style diversification will be key in 2002.  Given that
we expect major market averages to fluctuate by plus or minus
10%, stocks that beat those averages will have to offer a great deal
of weapons. Therefore, we are focusing on 10 stocks that we
believe will thrive across a broad range of styles, including growth,
value, and international. To smash the averages this year, we have
selected growth stocks that have outstanding earnings visibility and
dominant market positions, and value stocks with top, highly
disciplined management teams. We also offer investors a couple of
short ideas where heavy debt loads and technological obsolesce
