This transaction was a real pleasure to work on.  It is a 12 month 
all-requirements contract with Central Maine Power Company for their 
medium-sized commercial customers.

Once again the model of a cross-functional team was successfully employed.  
John Llodra was the lead originator with support from George Wood 
(mid-market), Janice Moore (legal) and myself.  The four of us participated 
in numerous meetings with both the counterparty and with the regulatory 
commission overseeing the procurement process with the ultimate result of 
having our contract approved and executed the same day.  I am told the deal 
booked $10m for ENA.



