otherwise we know the outcome to expect.

regarding your question on hourly day ahead markets -- I assume you're 
referring to the energy market that the PX used to run, because the CAISO 
already has day-ahead markets for congestion and ancillary services.  I 
discussed this proposal with Tim in March because the ISO's filing at FERC 
for market reforms had the ISO setting up such a market -- essentially 
putting the former PX inside the ISO (and for all you historians, finally 
creating the dream of POOLCO for California).  Tim asked us to oppose that 
proposal -- his view at the time was that we didn;t want the ISO running 
energY markets, because private third parties could do a much better job of 
that.  So, we opposed that in our filings commenting on the ISO's proposal in 
March.

